    {
      "id": "tgNq426r4a6Tn_d798vN3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -49291.44423890902,
      "y": -4870.0008766757655,
      "width": 916.33935546875,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1385387900,
      "version": 216,
      "versionNonce": 1757856508,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784210728611,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We don't want to fetch entire videos set, maintaining just 1000 top videos are fine\nWe don't want to allow user to query way back in time i.e. top k of last year's October month\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We don't want to fetch entire videos set, maintaining just 1000 top videos are fine\nWe don't want to allow user to query way back in time i.e. top k of last year's October month\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "C4rUqoLlN2zlwoTeeMwDl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -49284.16475495162,
      "y": -4748.97945588429,
      "width": 296.27978515625,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 407060804,
      "version": 199,
      "versionNonce": 2110970948,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784227714609,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Non-Functional Requirements\n- 1min delay to writes\n- No approximations\n- Massive number of views - ?\n- Massive number of videos - ?\n- Results in 10-100ms",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Non-Functional Requirements\n- 1min delay to writes\n- No approximations\n- Massive number of views - ?\n- Massive number of videos - ?\n- Results in 10-100ms",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "48aDTyCP7DMaO4w1taV5j",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -49276.885270994244,
      "y": -4528.775066173478,
      "width": 821.6994018554688,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 903457532,
      "version": 190,
      "versionNonce": 736383428,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784227860319,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Entities\n- Video\n- View\n- Time Window\n\n\nAPIs\n// retrive top k videos\nGET /views/top-k?window={WINDOW}&k={K} -> { videoId: string, views: number }[]\n\n- Here no pagination as we've limited the response max(k) = 1000 ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Entities\n- Video\n- View\n- Time Window\n\n\nAPIs\n// retrive top k videos\nGET /views/top-k?window={WINDOW}&k={K} -> { videoId: string, views: number }[]\n\n- Here no pagination as we've limited the response max(k) = 1000 ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lrhhnwZOZibas6lqGBAZy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -50052.26841133235,
      "y": -4214.021628863407,
      "width": 1572.1590576171875,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1671100484,
      "version": 1189,
      "versionNonce": 444528068,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784228660359,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes\n\nquery top k?\n- We assume the views to a video are pushed to a kafka stream by some other video team, we're just concerned about the view data that's in Kafka\n- They send the view data to this kafka topic - This assumption allows us to unnecessary not required to this problem entities \n- So ViewEvent topic is partitioned by videoId and there's a consumer service that pushes those views to PostgresDB\n    - The view consumer service retrieves a view event from the Kafka stream.\n    - The view consumer updates the counter for the video ID in the Postgres database.\n- Now have a different service Top-K Service that receives request from client, queries the Postgres DB for views and retuns.\n    SELECT \"videoId\", \"views\", \n    FROM VideoViews \n    ORDER BY \"views\" DESC LIMIT k;\n- Create index on views column\n- The problem is with every write we need to update the views index\n\n\nClients should be able to query tumbling window{hour, day, month}\n- View table has timestamp to it say hour of the view event, this means we'll have many rows for videos that have been viewed multiple times over several hours.\n- Lots of rows doesn't scale, but for now lets add index on the TS column\n    SELECT \"videoId\", SUM(\"views\") as \"views\", \n    FROM VideoViews \n    WHERE \"timestamp\" >= {windowStart} AND \"timestamp\" <= {windowEnd}\n    GROUP BY \"videoId\"\n    ORDER BY SUM(\"views\") DESC LIMIT {k};\n- Very inefficent query but okay for first draft",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Notes\n\nquery top k?\n- We assume the views to a video are pushed to a kafka stream by some other video team, we're just concerned about the view data that's in Kafka\n- They send the view data to this kafka topic - This assumption allows us to unnecessary not required to this problem entities \n- So ViewEvent topic is partitioned by videoId and there's a consumer service that pushes those views to PostgresDB\n    - The view consumer service retrieves a view event from the Kafka stream.\n    - The view consumer updates the counter for the video ID in the Postgres database.\n- Now have a different service Top-K Service that receives request from client, queries the Postgres DB for views and retuns.\n    SELECT \"videoId\", \"views\", \n    FROM VideoViews \n    ORDER BY \"views\" DESC LIMIT k;\n- Create index on views column\n- The problem is with every write we need to update the views index\n\n\nClients should be able to query tumbling window{hour, day, month}\n- View table has timestamp to it say hour of the view event, this means we'll have many rows for videos that have been viewed multiple times over several hours.\n- Lots of rows doesn't scale, but for now lets add index on the TS column\n    SELECT \"videoId\", SUM(\"views\") as \"views\", \n    FROM VideoViews \n    WHERE \"timestamp\" >= {windowStart} AND \"timestamp\" <= {windowEnd}\n    GROUP BY \"videoId\"\n    ORDER BY SUM(\"views\") DESC LIMIT {k};\n- Very inefficent query but okay for first draft",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pV6CHTzdZ7QQ0rj-JPhnK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -48256.52347921551,
      "y": -5353.905343426135,
      "width": 159.21492507804922,
      "height": 36.719337200474,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
